From e8f9566f8c00ca3518178b44f62782e13f0ab72c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joseph Tassarotti <jt4767@nyu.edu>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 02:52:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] raft: trace hooks under the goose tag (Goose translates the
 with_tla build)

The trace hooks' bodies (state_trace.go) are built under goose's build tag too, so that Goose
translates raft with its TLA+ trace instrumentation: etcd-grove's trace-validation proof (its
examples/raft/tracecheck) needs the hooks to report their events. Without a TraceLogger
(Config.TraceLogger nil, as every caller but a trace harness) the hooks return at once, as the
no-op build's.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 state_trace.go     | 2 +-
 state_trace_nop.go | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/state_trace.go b/state_trace.go
index caccd70..4aa175e 100644
--- a/state_trace.go
+++ b/state_trace.go
@@ -12,7 +12,7 @@
 // See the License for the specific language governing permissions and
 // limitations under the License.
 
-//go:build with_tla
+//go:build with_tla || goose
 
 package raft
 
diff --git a/state_trace_nop.go b/state_trace_nop.go
index f954c05..1203231 100644
--- a/state_trace_nop.go
+++ b/state_trace_nop.go
@@ -12,7 +12,7 @@
 // See the License for the specific language governing permissions and
 // limitations under the License.
 
-//go:build !with_tla
+//go:build !with_tla && !goose
 
 package raft
 
-- 
